    "Choosing a package for an Peradeniya wedding starts with the same questions as any booking — how many people, what level of detail for the groom, and whether the wider baraat needs full styling or a simpler coordinated look — but travel from Sri Lanka adds planning time worth building in. Because the team commits to a specific date and route for a Peradeniya assignment, package and quantity decisions are best finalised a week or two earlier than they would be for a local wedding, giving enough time to prepare fabric and confirm the final artist count. If your Peradeniya celebration includes multiple functions across a short trip, a combined package covering all of them is usually more practical than booking each date separately. We're glad to talk through a realistic package once we know your approximate headcount, the venue type, and whether the wedding is a single day or a multi-day stay — share what you have so far and we'll take it from there.",
